    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d22-a1">

                <pb facs="0132" n="26" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg26"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 184.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Kranz to Mr. Grant</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <p>Julius Kranz, United States citizen, passport No. 30838, of June 30, 1891, was
                    arrested by gens d’armes on the occasion of a visit he paid to his parents
                    residing here, his documents taken from him, and he was not set free before he
                    had given bail and agreed to appear before a board of examination on August 4,
                    1891. Requests speedy and active assistance and telegraphic orders for return of
                    documents and bail, as well as revokement of order to appear before the board of
                    enrollment on August 4.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Julius Kranz</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
